{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHotkeys(hotkeys, commonOptions?): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeys.ts#L73","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeys.ts:73"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue composable for registering multiple keyboard hotkeys at once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses the singleton HotkeyManager for efficient event handling.\nAccepts a dynamic array of hotkey definitions, making it safe to use\nwith variable-length lists."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hotkeys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkeys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeRefOrGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeyDefinition.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeyDefinition"}]},{"type":"text","value":"[]>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array of hotkey definitions to register, or a getter/ref"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"commonoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"commonOptions?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeRefOrGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeyOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeyOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared options applied to all hotkeys (overridden by per-definition options)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nuseHotkeys([\n  { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => save() },\n  { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => undo() },\n  { hotkey: 'Escape', callback: () => close() },\n])\n</script>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst items = computed(() => [...])\n// Dynamic hotkeys from reactive data\nuseHotkeys(\n  () => items.value.map((item) => ({\n    hotkey: item.shortcut,\n    callback: item.action,\n    options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n  })),\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)\n</script>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"hotkeys","text":"hotkeys","level":3},{"id":"commonoptions","text":"commonOptions?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeys(hotkeys, commonOptions?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeys.ts:73](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeys.ts#L73)\n\nVue composable for registering multiple keyboard hotkeys at once.\n\nUses the singleton HotkeyManager for efficient event handling.\nAccepts a dynamic array of hotkey definitions, making it safe to use\nwith variable-length lists.\n\nOptions are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkeys\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeyDefinition`](../interfaces/UseHotkeyDefinition.md)[]\\>\n\nArray of hotkey definitions to register, or a getter/ref\n\n### commonOptions?\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeyOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\nShared options applied to all hotkeys (overridden by per-definition options)\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nuseHotkeys([\n  { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => save() },\n  { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => undo() },\n  { hotkey: 'Escape', callback: () => close() },\n])\n</script>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst items = computed(() => [...])\n// Dynamic hotkeys from reactive data\nuseHotkeys(\n  () => items.value.map((item) => ({\n    hotkey: item.shortcut,\n    callback: item.action,\n    options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n  })),\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)\n</script>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHotkeys\ntitle: useHotkeys\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeys(hotkeys, commonOptions?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeys.ts:73](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeys.ts#L73)\n\nVue composable for registering multiple keyboard hotkeys at once.\n\nUses the singleton HotkeyManager for efficient event handling.\nAccepts a dynamic array of hotkey definitions, making it safe to use\nwith variable-length lists.\n\nOptions are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkeys\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeyDefinition`](../interfaces/UseHotkeyDefinition.md)[]\\>\n\nArray of hotkey definitions to register, or a getter/ref\n\n### commonOptions?\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeyOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\nShared options applied to all hotkeys (overridden by per-definition options)\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nuseHotkeys([\n  { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => save() },\n  { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => undo() },\n  { hotkey: 'Escape', callback: () => close() },\n])\n</script>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeys } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst items = computed(() => [...])\n// Dynamic hotkeys from reactive data\nuseHotkeys(\n  () => items.value.map((item) => ({\n    hotkey: item.shortcut,\n    callback: item.action,\n    options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n  })),\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)\n</script>\n```\n"}
